<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> a skos:ConceptScheme ; dct:title "How it is said to work"@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/body-clock> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Body clock timing"@en ;
  skos:definition "Sets or shifts the circadian clock: light at the right time, regular times, gradual shifts, melatonin timing."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/light-at-night> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Light at night"@en ;
  skos:definition "Less light in the evening or at night, said to keep melatonin up and the brain less alert."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/sleep-pressure> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Sleep pressure"@en ;
  skos:definition "Builds or protects the drive to sleep that grows the longer you are awake (naps, time in bed, activity)."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/body-temperature> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Body temperature"@en ;
  skos:definition "Helps the core body temperature drop that comes with sleep (cool room, warm bath then cooling, warm feet)."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/arousal> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Calming body and mind"@en ;
  skos:definition "Lowers mental, emotional or physical arousal: stress, racing thoughts, exciting content, hard exercise."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/learned-association> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Learned cues"@en ;
  skos:definition "Trains the brain to link bed and bedtime routines with sleep, not with lying awake."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/substances> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Substances"@en ;
  skos:definition "Caffeine, alcohol, nicotine, supplements, herbal products, medicines."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/digestion-and-fluids> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Food, drink and digestion"@en ;
  skos:definition "Meal timing and size, reflux, night-time bathroom trips."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/sleep-environment> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Bedroom environment"@en ;
  skos:definition "Noise, comfort, tidiness, scent: the room itself."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/breathing-and-airway> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Breathing and airway"@en ;
  skos:definition "Keeping the airway open at night; snoring and sleep apnea."@en .
<https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism/time-displacement> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:inScheme <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:topConceptOf <https://health-culture.org/sleep-advice/facet/mechanism> ;
  skos:prefLabel "Time taken from sleep"@en ;
  skos:definition "An activity that pushes bedtime later or eats into sleep time (e.g. screens, per Bauducco et al. 2024)."@en .
